course: dictionary
lesson: 637
title: Backside: a jokey word for your bottom
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Backside is an informal word for your bottom, the part of your body you sit on. It is a bit jokey and slightly rude, so you will hear it in everyday talk and funny stories, but you would not use it in a formal letter or a science report.
explain: Context helps you work out what it means. Look at the phrase «fall on your backside». The word tells you where the person landed, and it sounds funny because they fell down hard. Look for clues like this before you reach for a dictionary.
explain: Phrases can have meanings that are not about sitting at all. «Get off your backside» means stop being lazy and do something. If you read it literally, you would picture someone standing up from a chair, but the clue is that it is said to someone who is not doing their share.
explain: Backside has a rare second meaning: the back part of something, as in «the backside of the building». In maths and science lessons, say "back" or "rear" instead.
fact: Backside means your bottom, and it is informal.
fact: Backside is a bit rude, so use it with care, and say "bottom" in formal writing.
fact: «Get off your backside» means stop being lazy and do something.
fact: «A pain in the backside» means an annoying person or thing, and it is rude.
fact: In maths and science, say "back" or "rear" instead of backside.
exercise: What does the phrase «fall on your backside» mean? | To sneeze very loudly | *To land on your bottom | To win a race | To fall over the front of a bike
exercise: «Get off your backside» means what? | *Stop being lazy and do something | Sit down and rest | Stand up very fast | Leave the room quietly
exercise: Which word would a scientist use instead of backside for the back end of a rocket? | Spine | Bum | *Rear | Hips
test: «A pain in the backside» means what? | A kind friend | *An annoying person or thing | A bad headache | A sore bottom from sitting too long
test: Which is the rare meaning of backside? | Your bottom | A lazy person | *The back part of something, like the backside of a building | A loud noise
exam: Which word is the most formal choice for a school report about a fall? | Backside | *Bottom | Butt | Bum
